       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and the analgesic benefit doesn't increase.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common prescription anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum under medical supervision\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), a typical analgesic regimen\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided as 400 mg PO four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it now."
